[EVENTREG v90.2.5.4] Event report AI floor 77->82 - Bronson Reed is clearly not wasting time while away from WWE television. The RAW star took to X with a new photo showing off a noticeably bigger and more shredded physique while continuing his recovery from injury. Reed kept the message short and confident with a simple caption. "Break the internet." The post immediately got fans talking as Reed appeared to be in incredible shape despite still being sidelined from WWE programming. Reed has been absent from RAW since suffering a torn distal biceps in his right arm during a February episode of the show. WWE has not confirmed when he will be cleared to return to action. Before the injury, Reed had been working as part of The Vision faction alongside Logan Paul and Austin Theory. The group remains active on RAW, with Logan Paul and Theory currently holding the World Tag Team Championship after retaining their titles against The Street Profits at Saturday Night's Main Event. Bron Breakker has mostly handled singles duties for The Vision during Reed's absence, including stepping up during the group's recent appearances on RAW and SNME. Now, based on his latest photo, Bronson Reed looks more than ready to make an impact once he finally returns to WWE television. What do you think about Bronson Reed's new look during his WWE absence? Let us know your thoughts and feedback in the comments below. Derek Holloway is a writer at Ringside News specializing in professional wrestling news, rumors, and results. He focuses on delivering reliable coverage across WWE, AEW, and major wrestling promotions.
